-## Append to a note
+For a **Daily Note** (YYYY-MM-DD format, common in Obsidian):
 
 ```bash
 VAULT="${OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH:-$HOME/Documents/Obsidian Vault}"
-echo "
-New content here." >> "$VAULT/Existing Note.md"
+DATE=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
+cat > "$VAULT/Daily/$DATE.md" << ENDNOTE
+# $DATE
+
+## Tasks
+
+- 
+
+## Notes
+
+ENDNOTE
+```
+
+## Append to a Note
+
+```bash
+VAULT="${OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH:-$HOME/Documents/Obsidian Vault}"
+printf '\n## New Section\n\nContent here.\n' >> "$VAULT/Existing Note.md"
 ```
 
 ## Wikilinks
 
-Obsidian links notes with `[[Note Name]]` syntax. When creating notes, use these to link related content.
+Obsidian links notes with `[[Note Name]]` syntax. When creating notes, use these to link related content:
+
+```markdown
+See also: [[Project Alpha]], [[Meeting 2026-04-11]]
+```
+
+Wikilinks do **not** require the `.md` extension. The note must exist (or Obsidian will show it as an unresolved link).
+
+## Pitfalls
+
+- **Vault path spaces**: Always quote `"$VAULT/Note.md"` — unquoted paths with spaces cause `cat: Obsidian: No such file or directory` errors.
+- **OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH unset**: If not set in `~/.hermes/.env`, the default `~/Documents/Obsidian Vault` may not exist. Check first with `ls "$VAULT"`.
+- **Overwriting vs appending**: Use `cat >` to overwrite, `>>` to append. Never overwrite unless certain the user wants to replace the full note.
+- **Subfolder must exist**: `cat > "$VAULT/Projects/NewNote.md"` fails if `Projects/` doesn't exist. Create it first: `mkdir -p "$VAULT/Projects"`.
+- **Wikilink case sensitivity**: Obsidian on macOS is case-insensitive, but Linux vaults are case-sensitive — `[[Meeting Notes]]` ≠ `[[meeting notes]]` on Linux.
+- **Binary/attachment files**: The vault may contain images, PDFs, and other attachments. Use `find "$VAULT" -name "*.md"` to restrict to notes only.
